Chapter: DiskInspector
  cites Dev chapter HexFormat
  cites Kernel chapter DiskFacts
  cites Foreword chapter FactLog
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 THE STORE NO LONGER STARTS AT SECTOR ZERO, and that is why every command
 here resolves the region before it reads anything. The fact store lives
 in a partition of its own type and addresses every sector relative to
 that partition's base; on the shipped 16 MB image the base is 28639. A
 superblock decode pointed at LBA 0 therefore reads the protective MBR and
 reports no superblock about a disk that has one. The design this chapter
 implements still describes that command as reading sectors 0 and 1, which
 was true before the partition existed and is not true now.

 EVERY SECTOR READ COSTS 512 BYTES OF HEAP THAT IS NEVER RETURNED.
 `block-read-sector` is three instructions over the bump allocator: it
 takes the current heap pointer as its destination and advances the heap
 register by 512. Two consequences, and both shape the code below. A
 comparison needs no snapshot, because two reads land on two distinct
 buffers. And a walk of N entries costs 512N bytes until the calling
 function returns, which is why the walk is fuel-capped rather than
 running to the log head unconditionally.

 We say:

Section: The Region

  di-region-line : DiskRegion -> Text
  di-region-line (r) =
    if r.dr-base == fact-base-refuse then "region: REFUSED -- partition table with no fact partition"
    else if r.dr-base == fact-base-whole-disk then "region: whole disk, base 0 (unpartitioned)"
    else "region: base " & show (r.dr-base) & ", " & show (r.dr-limit) & " sectors"

Section: The Medium

  di-sector-count-line : [Device.Block] Text
  di-sector-count-line = act
    n <- block-sector-count
    if n <= 0 then "no disk attached (0 sectors)" else show n & " sectors, " & show (n / 2) & " KB"
  end

Section: One Sector

  di-sector-lines : Integer -> [Device.Block] List Text
  di-sector-lines (lba) = act
    buf <- (block-read-sector lba)
    (["LBA " & show lba] & hex-dump-lines buf 0 0 fl-sector-size)
  end

Section: Two Sectors

  di-compare-line : Integer, Integer -> [Device.Block] Text
  di-compare-line (x) (y) = act
    bx <- (block-read-sector x)
    by <- (block-read-sector y)
    (di-compare-loop bx by 0)
  end

  di-compare-loop : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  di-compare-loop (x) (y) (i) =
    if i >= fl-sector-size then "identical over " & show fl-sector-size & " bytes"
    else if peek-byte x i /= peek-byte y i then di-compare-diff x y i
    else di-compare-loop x y (i + 1)

  di-compare-diff : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  di-compare-diff (x) (y) (i) =
    "differ at +" & show i & ": " & hexfmt-byte-to-hex (peek-byte x i) & " vs " & hexfmt-byte-to-hex (peek-byte y i)

Section: The Superblock

  di-superblock-line : Superblock -> Text
  di-superblock-line (sb) =
    "log-head " & show (sb.log-head) & ", facts " & show (sb.fact-count) & ", gen " & show (sb.index-gen)

  di-superblock-lines : DiskRegion -> List Text
  di-superblock-lines (r) =
    if r.dr-base == fact-base-refuse then [di-region-line r]
    else when read-superblock (r.dr-base)
      is None -> [di-region-line r, "no superblock at base " & show (r.dr-base)]
      is Just (sb) -> [di-region-line r, di-superblock-line sb]

  di-superblock-report : List Text
  di-superblock-report = di-superblock-lines fact-store-region

Section: The Fact Log

 The walk reads HEADERS and never entry content. `scan-fact-at` is the
 obvious primitive and it is the wrong one here: it calls
 `disk-read-entry-content`, which allocates a buffer the size of the whole
 fact and materialises it, so listing a log would cost the log. Kind,
 length and timestamp are all in the entry's first sector, which the walk
 has already paid for.

  di-fact-line : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Text
  di-fact-line (sector) (buf) (clen) (nsec) =
    "+" & show sector & "  kind " & show (fl-entry-kind buf) & "  len " & show clen & "  " & show nsec & " sec  ts " & show (fl-entry-timestamp buf)

  di-facts-lines : DiskRegion, Integer, Integer, Integer -> List Text
  di-facts-lines (r) (sector) (end-sector) (fuel) =
    if fuel <= 0 then ["(truncated at sector " & show sector & ": fuel exhausted)"]
    else if sector >= end-sector then []
    else let buf = fact-read-at (r.dr-base) sector
    in let clen = fl-entry-content-len buf
    in if clen == 0 then []
    else let nsec = sectors-for-fact clen
    in [di-fact-line sector buf clen nsec] & di-facts-lines r (sector + nsec) end-sector (fuel - 1)

  di-facts-report : Integer -> List Text
  di-facts-report (fuel) =
    let r = fact-store-region
    in if r.dr-base == fact-base-refuse then [di-region-line r]
    else when read-superblock (r.dr-base)
      is None -> [di-region-line r, "no superblock at base " & show (r.dr-base)]
      is Just (sb) -> [di-region-line r] & di-facts-lines r fl-fact-log-start (sb.log-head) fuel
